Encapsulation is the process of bundling the data (variables) and the methods (functions) that operate on the data into a single unit, or class. It also restricts direct access to some components of an object, which is called **data hiding**.

### Purpose:
- To protect the internal state of an object.
- To prevent unintended interference and misuse of data.
- To make the code more modular and maintainable.

